cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: >-
  Beyond the Chomsky Wall: Platonic Representations as the
  Convergence Point of Natural Language and Code
# Legal authorship credit per academic convention (Paper-layer identity
# exception; see ~/IdeaProjects/Paper/CLAUDE.md). Public/portfolio surfaces
# use the Heznpc identity; this academic metadata file uses the legal name.
authors:
  - family-names: Yoon
    given-names: Jiyeon
abstract: >-
  Position paper arguing that the gap between natural language and programming
  language is not a barrier but a measurable, shrinking quantity — the Z-Gap —
  predicted to converge under the Platonic Representation Hypothesis. The work
  refines PRH by distinguishing representational convergence from
  communicability, stratifying the shared latent into semantic, procedural, and
  pragmatic layers, and reporting a cross-lingual NL-code alignment pilot across
  seven embedding models and five languages.
keywords:
  - representation learning
  - Platonic Representation Hypothesis
  - natural language
  - programming language
  - cross-lingual invariance
  - disambiguation cost
license: CC-BY-4.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/heznpc/z-gap"
